    "All fractions and distance summaries are row-weighted descriptive statistics, not validation scores or estimates of held-out Recall@50.",
    "Location centers use deduplicated item metadata, training rows preferred when an item is repeated across train and corpus. Latitude/longitude values are converted to floats and invalid/zero pairs are excluded from center estimation.",
    "Service fields are parsed heuristically, then restricted to frequent clean field values. The literal label Вид услуги without a value is not a useful service constraint.",
    "Identification of regional versus city versus nationwide search scope is an inference from observed positive pairs, not an official geographic lookup.",
    "Coordinates can have extreme outliers: even exact-location positive pairs include distances over 10000 km. Distances must remain soft features.",
    "Candidate allocation such as 30 local + 10 nearby + 10 global is only an initial validation experiment, not a measured optimum. For region or national scope select pools dynamically from learned location distributions."
